---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { supportEmail } from '../site.js';

/* The date the text below last changed in substance. Moving it is part of
   changing the policy, and section 14 says how a change is announced. */
const updated = '2 October 2026';
---

<Base
	title="Privacy Policy — Teachouse"
	description="What Teachouse collects, why, where it is kept, who else sees it, and how to get it corrected or deleted."
>
	<section class="section">
		<div class="wrap prose policy">
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p class="policy-meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

			<p>
				Teachouse helps teachers who sell resources keep one catalogue and publish it to several
				marketplaces. This policy explains what personal information we collect when you use the
				Teachouse website, the web console and the Teachouse app on your computer or phone, what we
				do with it, and the choices you have.
			</p>
			<p>
				"Teachouse", "we" and "us" mean the business that runs Teachouse in New Zealand.
				"You" means the person who holds a Teachouse account, or anyone visiting our website.
			</p>

			<h2 id="summary">At a glance</h2>
			<div class="policy-scroll">
				<table class="policy-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">What</th>
							<th scope="col">Why we have it</th>
							<th scope="col">Where it is kept</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Your name, email and sign-in details</th>
							<td>To create your account and let you sign in</td>
							<td>Our servers in New Zealand</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Your catalogue: titles, descriptions, prices, covers</th>
							<td>It is the product: we keep it so you can publish it</td>
							<td>Our servers in New Zealand, files encrypted</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Files you import from a marketplace</th>
							<td>So you can open and publish them again</td>
							<td>On your own devices only, encrypted</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Your marketplace passwords and logins</th>
							<td>Signing in to marketplaces happens in the app on your device</td>
							<td>On your own device only. We never receive them</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Card details</th>
							<td>To take payment</td>
							<td>With Stripe only. We never see them</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">How the console is used</th>
							<td>To find what is confusing or broken</td>
							<td>PostHog, in the European Union</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Security records: sign-ins, IP address, browser</th>
							<td>To protect your account and investigate problems</td>
							<td>Our servers in New Zealand</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				We do not sell personal information, we do not use it for advertising, and we do not share
				it with anyone except the service providers listed in{' '}
				<a class="link" href="#sharing">section 5</a>.
			</p>

			<nav class="policy-toc" aria-label="Sections of this policy">
				<ol>
					<li><a href="#collect">What we collect</a></li>
					<li><a href="#never">What we never collect</a></li>
					<li><a href="#use">How we use it</a></li>
					<li><a href="#bases">Legal bases (EU and UK)</a></li>
					<li><a href="#sharing">Who else sees it</a></li>
					<li><a href="#location">Where it is kept</a></li>
					<li><a href="#retention">How long we keep it</a></li>
					<li><a href="#security">How we protect it</a></li>
					<li><a href="#cookies">Cookies and browser storage</a></li>
					<li><a href="#rights">Your rights</a></li>
					<li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
					<li><a href="#breach">If something goes wrong</a></li>
					<li><a href="#law">Governing law and complaints</a></li>
					<li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
					<li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
				</ol>
			</nav>

			<h2 id="collect">1. What we collect</h2>

			<h3>Your account</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Your name and email address, and the email address you choose for notices if it is a
					different one.
				</li>
				<li>
					How you sign in: a password, stored only as a one-way hash we cannot turn back into the
					password; a passkey, of which we hold only the public half, while the private half stays
					on your device; or a Google or Microsoft account, in which case that provider tells us
					your name, email address and whether the address is verified.
				</li>
				<li>
					Your signed-in sessions: when each started and expires, the IP address and the browser it
					came from.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>Your organisation and catalogue</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Your account settings, organisation name, plan and the marketplaces you connect.
				</li>
				<li>
					The resources you create or import: titles, descriptions, prices, grades, subjects, tags,
					cover images and thumbnails, the files you upload through the console, and the choices
					you make about where each resource is published.
				</li>
				<li>
					What happened when you published: which listing went where and when, and whether it
					worked. We also keep the sales and view figures a marketplace reports back to you, so you
					can see them over time.
				</li>
				<li>
					Your permission to use a marketplace that has no official connection, with the date you
					gave or withdrew it.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>Your devices</h3>
			<p>
				The Teachouse app on your computer or phone does the work that has to happen under your own
				marketplace login. For each device you sign in, we keep a name for it, which marketplaces it
				is signed in to, when it last checked in, and the network address other devices of yours
				use to reach it. We also keep a list of which files each device holds, identified by a
				fingerprint of the file's contents and its name, never the file itself.
			</p>
			<p>
				Files you import from a marketplace stay on your devices, encrypted with a key that never
				leaves that device. When one of your devices needs a copy of a file another of your devices
				holds, the two connect to each other directly over an encrypted connection. The file does
				not pass through our servers.
			</p>
			<p>
				Files you import from a marketplace stay on your own devices: when you open one in the
				console, Teachouse passes it from your device to your browser without keeping it. Files you
				upload to Teachouse yourself are stored by Teachouse so you can use them anywhere, until you
				delete them.
			</p>

			<h3>Billing</h3>
			<p>
				If you buy a plan or a pack, you pay on Stripe's checkout page, and Stripe collects your card
				details and billing address. We receive and keep your Stripe customer reference, what you
				bought, the amount, the currency, the tax charged, your invoices, and whether payment
				succeeded.
			</p>

			<h3>How you use Teachouse</h3>
			<p>
				When you use the website or console, we record page views and a small set of named events,
				such as starting a checkout or finishing an import, with counts and settings rather than
				anything you wrote. In the console these are linked to your organisation, not to you by
				name or email address. We also record sessions of the console so we can see where people
				get stuck; every text field and every piece of text on the page is masked before it is
				recorded, so the recording shows the layout, not your catalogue. The website records page
				views only and never records sessions.
			</p>

			<h3>Technical and security records</h3>
			<p>
				Our servers record requests and errors so we can keep Teachouse running. Our sign-in
				service keeps a security log of sign-ups, sign-ins, failed sign-ins, sign-outs and password
				resets, with the IP address and browser of each. When a sign-in fails or a password reset is
				requested, that log holds the email address that was typed, because there is no account to
				name instead.
			</p>

			<h3>Messages</h3>
			<p>
				If you write to us or send a request through the console, such as asking for a new
				marketplace, we keep what you sent and our reply.
			</p>

			<h2 id="never">2. What we never collect</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Your marketplace passwords or login sessions for marketplaces without an official
					connection. You sign in to those inside the Teachouse app on your own device; the login is
					kept in your device's own secure storage and our servers never receive it.
				</li>
				<li>Your card number or bank details. Those go straight to Stripe.</li>
				<li>
					Information about your buyers, beyond the sales totals a marketplace shows you.
				</li>
				<li>Anything from the files you import, other than their name and fingerprint.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Some marketplaces offer an official connection for tools like Teachouse. When we connect to
				one of those for you, we will hold the access token that marketplace issues, use it only
				from our servers to act on your listings, and delete it when you disconnect. The
				marketplaces Teachouse connects to today do not offer one, so their sign-in stays on your
				device.
			</p>

			<h2 id="use">3. How we use it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>To run your account, sign you in, and keep your catalogue.</li>
				<li>To publish, update and track your listings where you ask us to.</li>
				<li>To take payment and apply your plan.</li>
				<li>
					To send you email you need: verifying your address, resetting your password, telling you
					your password changed, and telling you when an import or a publish has finished or needs
					you. We do not send marketing email.
				</li>
				<li>To stop abuse, such as automated sign-ups, and to keep accounts secure.</li>
				<li>To find and fix problems, and to understand which parts of Teachouse are used.</li>
				<li>To answer you when you contact us.</li>
				<li>To meet legal duties, such as keeping tax records.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				If you ask us for help, a Teachouse administrator may view your account as you see it, to
				find the problem. Every time that happens it is recorded, with which administrator it was
				and when.
			</p>

			<h2 id="bases">4. Legal bases (EU and UK)</h2>
			<p>
				If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, the law requires us to say
				why we are allowed to use your information:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Contract:</strong> your account, catalogue, devices, publishing, billing and the
					email that goes with them. We cannot provide Teachouse without them.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Legitimate interests:</strong> security records, stopping abuse, and product
					analytics. We keep these to what we need, and you can object (see{' '}
					<a class="link" href="#rights">section 10</a>).
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Consent:</strong> connecting a marketplace that has no official connection. You
					can withdraw it at any time from your account.
				</li>
				<li><strong>Legal obligation:</strong> tax and accounting records.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="sharing">5. Who else sees it</h2>
			<p>
				We use a small number of service providers. Each one receives only what it needs for its
				job, and may use it only to provide that service to us.
			</p>
			<div class="policy-scroll">
				<table class="policy-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Provider</th>
							<th scope="col">What it does for us</th>
							<th scope="col">What it receives</th>
							<th scope="col">Where</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Cloudflare</th>
							<td>Delivers our website and blocks automated sign-ups (Turnstile)</td>
							<td>Your IP address, browser details and the pages you request</td>
							<td>Global network</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Stripe</th>
							<td>Takes payment and runs the billing page</td>
							<td>Your email address, payment details and what you buy</td>
							<td>United States and elsewhere</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Resend</th>
							<td>Sends our email</td>
							<td>Your email address, name and the message</td>
							<td>United States</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">PostHog</th>
							<td>Product analytics</td>
							<td>
								Page views, named events and masked session recordings, linked to your organisation's
								ID
							</td>
							<td>European Union</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Have I Been Pwned</th>
							<td>Warns you if a new password has appeared in a known data breach</td>
							<td>
								The first five characters of a one-way hash of the password, never the password
							</td>
							<td>Global network</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Google, Microsoft</th>
							<td>Sign-in, only if you choose it</td>
							<td>The fact that you are signing in to Teachouse</td>
							<td>Their own locations</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				When you publish, the marketplace you publish to receives your listing: that is the point.
				What it does with it is covered by that marketplace's own privacy policy.
			</p>
			<p>
				We may also disclose information if the law requires it, to protect someone's safety, or to
				a buyer of the business if Teachouse is sold, in which case this policy continues to apply
				to your information.
			</p>

			<h2 id="location">6. Where it is kept</h2>
			<p>
				Your account and catalogue are stored on servers we run in New Zealand, and so are our
				backups. Product analytics are stored by PostHog in the European Union. Cloudflare, Stripe
				and Resend may process information in other countries, including the United States.
			</p>
			<p>
				New Zealand is recognised by the European Commission and the United Kingdom as giving
				adequate protection to personal information. Where a provider handles information from the
				EU or UK outside those places, we rely on its standard contractual clauses or an equivalent
				safeguard.
			</p>

			<h2 id="retention">7. How long we keep it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Your account and catalogue:</strong> for as long as your account is open. When
					your account is deleted, they are deleted with it.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Sessions:</strong> a console session lasts up to 7 days, and ends sooner if you
					sign out.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Progress of imports and publishes:</strong> the step-by-step record is deleted
					after 30 days. The result of each publish stays with your catalogue.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Security log and server logs:</strong> kept only as long as we need them to
					investigate problems and protect accounts.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Billing records:</strong> kept for as long as tax law requires, which in New
					Zealand is seven years.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Backups:</strong> encrypted, and replaced on a rolling schedule. The oldest is 12
					months old, so information deleted from Teachouse is gone from every backup within 12
					months.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Files on your devices:</strong> under your control. Deleting a resource in
					Teachouse does not delete your copy of the file; delete it yourself if you want it gone.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2 id="security">8. How we protect it</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>Every connection to Teachouse is encrypted with TLS.</li>
				<li>
					Files and images we store are encrypted, each under its own key, and those keys are
					themselves encrypted under a master key kept apart from the files.
				</li>
				<li>
					Our database separates every organisation's rows at the database level, so a request made
					for one account cannot read another's.
				</li>
				<li>
					Passwords are stored as one-way hashes, and passkeys are supported as a stronger
					alternative.
				</li>
				<li>
					Marketplace logins and imported files on your devices are kept in the device's own
					secure storage and encrypted on disk.
				</li>
				<li>
					You can see which devices are signed in to your account and sign any of them out. A
					signed-out device deletes its marketplace logins the next time it connects.
				</li>
				<li>Only a small number of administrators can reach account data, and their access is logged.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>No system is perfectly secure, but we design Teachouse to hold as little as it can.</p>

			<h2 id="cookies">9. Cookies and browser storage</h2>
			<p>
				Every cookie and every item of browser storage below is set on Teachouse's own address. We
				do not use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies, and we do not load other companies'
				trackers. Analytics reach PostHog through our own address, so your browser never talks to
				PostHog directly.
			</p>
			<div class="policy-scroll">
				<table class="policy-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Name</th>
							<th scope="col">What it is for</th>
							<th scope="col">How long</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>tam_session</code></th>
							<td>Keeps you signed in to the console. Required.</td>
							<td>Up to 7 days</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>better-auth.…</code></th>
							<td>Our sign-in service's own session, which signs you in to the console. Required.</td>
							<td>Until the session ends</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>cf_clearance</code></th>
							<td>
								Set by Cloudflare, which runs our network edge, to show your browser passed its
								check against automated traffic. Required.
							</td>
							<td>Set by Cloudflare, usually minutes to hours</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row"><code>teachouse.theme</code></th>
							<td>Remembers light or dark mode (browser storage, not a cookie).</td>
							<td>Until you clear it</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">Other <code>teachouse.…</code> items</th>
							<td>
								Browser storage for console preferences and steps in progress, such as the plan you
								picked before signing up. Never sent to anyone.
							</td>
							<td>Until you clear it, or the step finishes</td>
						</tr>
						<tr>
							<th scope="row">PostHog (<code>ph_…</code>)</th>
							<td>
								A random identifier so analytics can tell one visit from the next. Set on
								Teachouse's own address.
							</td>
							<td>Up to 1 year</td>
						</tr>
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p>
				The Turnstile check on the sign-in and sign-up pages runs in a frame served by Cloudflare,
				to tell people from automated programs. You can block cookies in your browser, but you will not be able to
				sign in without the required ones.
			</p>

			<h2 id="rights">10. Your rights</h2>
			<p>Wherever you live, you can ask us to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Access</strong> the personal information we hold about you.</li>
				<li><strong>Correct</strong> anything that is wrong.</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Export</strong> your catalogue. You can download it yourself as a spreadsheet from
					the console, and ask us for the rest.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Delete</strong> your account and everything in it. We confirm the request came
					from you, then delete the account, your organisation, your catalogue, your sessions and
					your sign-in details. The keys to your stored files are destroyed at the same time, so
					any copy left behind cannot be read. If you have a paid plan, cancel it first, or ask us
					to.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Object</strong> to analytics or <strong>restrict</strong> how we use your
					information.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Withdraw consent</strong> for a marketplace without an official connection, from
					your account at any time.
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				You can change your name and notice address yourself in Account settings. For anything
				else, contact us (<a class="link" href="#contact">section 15</a>). We answer within 20
				working days, as the New Zealand Privacy Act requires, and within one month if you are in
				the EU or UK. We do not charge for a request, and we will never treat you differently for
				making one.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you are in California, you have the rights above under the California Consumer Privacy
				Act. We do not sell or share personal information for cross-context behavioural
				advertising.
			</p>

			<h2 id="children">11. Children</h2>
			<p>
				Teachouse is a tool for teachers who sell teaching resources, not for students. You must be
				at least 18 to create or use an account, as our <a class="link" href="/terms/">Terms</a> say.
				We do not knowingly collect information from anyone under 18. If you believe a child has
				given us their information, contact us and we will delete it.
			</p>

			<h2 id="breach">12. If something goes wrong</h2>
			<p>
				If personal information we hold is lost, accessed or disclosed without permission and it is
				likely to cause serious harm, we will tell the people affected and the New Zealand Privacy
				Commissioner as soon as we practicably can. Where EU or UK law applies, we will notify the
				relevant authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of it.
			</p>

			<h2 id="law">13. Governing law and complaints</h2>
			<p>
				This policy is governed by the law of New Zealand, including the Privacy Act 2020. We also
				follow the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation for people in those places.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you are unhappy with how we have handled your information, please tell us first so we can
				put it right. You can also complain to the{' '}
				<a class="link" href="https://www.privacy.org.nz/">New Zealand Privacy Commissioner</a>, or
				to the data protection authority where you live.
			</p>

			<h2 id="changes">14. Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				When we change this policy, we update the date at the top. If a change affects how we use
				information we already hold, we will email account holders before it takes effect.
			</p>

			<h2 id="contact">15. Contact</h2>
			<p>
				For privacy questions and requests, email{' '}
				<a class="link" href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.
			</p>
			<p>
				This policy works alongside our <a class="link" href="/terms/">Terms</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
